description:
WHAT HAPPENED (run 01M2Y052A16VSYQFSC46H090HE, implementer@1 painpoint, rescued from the stranded run journal 2026-09-20): re-invoking `ml record` with the SAME --name upserts by name and silently REPLACES description/resolution — an id-probe invocation with 'noop' placeholder content overwrote the real record mx-526f86. On success the CLI prints no mx-id; the id must be scraped from .mulch/expertise/<domain>.jsonl. A subsequent --force re-record appended a NEAR-DUPLICATE line (differing only in recorded_at) under the SAME id mx-cbf108, which had to be deduped by hand.

DEMAND (acceptance):
- upsert-by-name REJECTS content-shrinking or placeholder amendments (or requires an explicit --amend flag) instead of silently replacing;
- `ml record` prints the mx-id on success;
- --force never appends a second line under an existing id (amend in place or fail);
- AGENTS.md mulch quick-reference gains the missing --resolution requirement for --type failure records (run 01M2XSA56XFSQPH3PAM4KXZCGY planner painpoint: first attempt failed with a copy-paste retry hint because the example omits it).

Analyzer pre-check: sd search found only fabro-c271 (shell-quoting hazard) and closed fabro-fe6f (dedup filings) — different defects. Basis: runs 01M2Y052A16VSYQFSC46H090HE + 01M2XSA56XFSQPH3PAM4KXZCGY (journals rescued to .fabro/journal/ via `/integrate` 2026-09-20), records mx-526f86 / mx-cbf108.
